      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the system itself feels broken, then trying to fix your place within it is just adding more labor to a dead end. When everything feels meaningless, the point of trying to detach is simply to reclaim the one thing the machine can't take: your own quiet space. Letting the machine fail sounds like a tempting surrender, but true freedom is found in choosing your own exit strategy, even if that exit is just a quiet pause.",
      "source": "target",
